<< /AP << /N 448 0 R >> /BS 40 0 R /Contents (In \(i\) many students forgot about the constant of integration.\rIn \(ii\) a common error was to let E=V0.\rIn \(iii\) most who got the quadratic equation did not check the solutions.  Half a mark was \rgiven for knowing that v=0.) /CreationDate (D:20160615133915+10'00') /DA (13.75 TL /Cour 10 Tf) /DS (font: Helv 10.0pt;font-stretch:Normal; text-align:left; color:#000000 ) /F 4 /IT /FreeTextTypewriter /M (D:20160615134135+10'00') /NM (a068db03-23b2-40e8-8d54-7a4e1ff19a09) /P 311 0 R /RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:11.0.16" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;font-family:Helv;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="line-height:13.8pt;font-family:Helvetica">In \(i\) many students forgot about the constant of integration.&#13;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="line-height:13.8pt;font-family:Helvetica">In \(ii\) a common error was to let E=V0.&#13;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="line-height:13.8pt;font-family:Helvetica">In \(iii\) most who got the quadratic equation did not check the solutions.  Half a mark was &#13;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="line-height:13.8pt;font-family:Helvetica">given for knowing that v=0.</span></p></body>) /Rect [ 34.6396 91.0056 423.737 146.016 ] /Subj (Typewritten Text) /Subtype /FreeText /T (kilmoreb) /Type /Annot >>
[ 319 0 R ]
<< /AP << /N 449 0 R >> /BS 40 0 R /Contents (The most common error in \(d\) was that students were trying to differentiate a formula with respect to\rtwo variables. The other common mistake was to substitute in h-=5 at the start of the problem.) /CreationDate (D:20160615134135+10'00') /DA (13.75 TL /Cour 10 Tf) /DS (font: Helv 10.0pt;font-stretch:Normal; text-align:left; color:#000000 ) /F 4 /IT /FreeTextTypewriter /M (D:20160615134329+10'00') /NM (9a93967e-e2ba-4b44-81cb-2d497247c159) /P 313 0 R /RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:11.0.16" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;font-family:Helv;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="line-height:13.8pt;font-family:Helvetica">The most common error in \(d\) was that students were trying to differentiate a formula with respect to&#13;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="line-height:13.8pt;font-family:Helvetica">two variables. The other common mistake was to substitute in h-=5 at the start of the problem.</span></p></body>) /Rect [ 33.1656 222.425 475.584 249.935 ] /Subj (Typewritten Text) /Subtype /FreeText /T (kilmoreb) /Type /Annot >>
